---
title: Active pending invite uniqueness invariant
description: Domain rule — at most one INVITED row per (tenantId, normalized phone) on POST /users/invite.
---

# Active pending invite uniqueness invariant

```yaml
id: INVITE-ACTIVE-UNIQUENESS-INVARIANT
version: "2026-08-20"
status: LOCKED
authority: users-rbac.policy.ts · in-memory/prisma identity repositories · users.service.ts
decisions: [DEC-P9-015, DEC-P9-018]
related:
  - subphases/9.4-users-rbac.md
  - users-api-dispatch-addendum.md
  - invite-accept-membership-invariant.mdoc
```

## Problem

`POST /users/invite` always inserted a new `OperatorPendingInvite` row. Same workspace could accumulate multiple **INVITED** rows for one normalized phone — ambiguous queue, duplicate OTP paths, noisy directory.

## Rule (domain)

**Scope:** `(tenantId, normalizedPhone)` where `status = INVITED`.

**Active** means the row is listed by `findPendingInviteByPhone` / `GET /users/invites` (status `INVITED` only). Revoked rows are **deleted** (not a secondary status today). Accepted rows are **deleted** on consume.

```text
existing INVITED row for (tenantId, normalizeLoginMobile(phone))?
  no  → create pending invite (201)
  yes → reject; do not insert; return 409 INVITE_ALREADY_PENDING with existing inviteId
```

Phone normalization uses the same path as login and accept: `normalizeLoginMobile` → `canonicalizeLoginMobile` (e.g. `0912…` and `+98912…` resolve to one key).

Evaluated by `evaluateInviteCreate` in `users-rbac.policy.ts`. Enforced inside **`createPendingInvite`** on both identity repositories (write boundary). Not a controller-only check.

### Case table

| Case | Decision | HTTP | Code |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ---- |
| No active invite | **Allow** — insert row | **201** | — |
| Active invite exists (same tenant + normalized phone) | **Reject** — no second row | **409** | `INVITE_ALREADY_PENDING` |
| Same phone, different tenant | **Allow** — tenant isolation | **201** | — |
| Prior invite revoked or accepted (row gone) | **Allow** — no active row | **201** | — |
| Existing workspace membership | **Unchanged** — invite create does not mutate `UserTenant` (P0 accept invariant separate) | — | — |

## Concurrency

Two concurrent `POST /users/invite` for the same `(tenantId, phone)` must not leave two active rows.

| Driver | Mechanism |
| ------ | --------- |
| Memory | Single-threaded check + insert in `createPendingInvite`; secondary index `invitesByTenantPhone` |
| Prisma | Transaction + `pg_advisory_xact_lock(hashtext(tenantId:phone))` then `findFirst` + `create` |

Future P1 may add a partial unique index `(tenantId, phone) WHERE status = 'INVITED'`; this phase does **not** add migrations.

## Non-goals (this change)

- No invite TTL / expiry status (P1 follow-up).
- No UI or route changes.
- No permission model changes.
- No second invite subsystem.

## Sequence

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant S as inviteWorkspaceUser
  participant R as createPendingInvite
  participant P as evaluateInviteCreate
  S->>R: tenantId + normalized phone
  R->>R: lock / index lookup
  R->>P: existing INVITED row?
  alt duplicate
    P-->>R: INVITE_ALREADY_PENDING
    R-->>S: throw InviteAlreadyPendingError
  else allow
    R->>R: insert invite
    R-->>S: PendingInviteRecord
  end
```
